# The shared pre-push: this repo's own `check`, narrowed to what the push can affect.
#
# ★ `bun test` runs only the test files the pushed changes can reach (Bun's --changed),
#   `lint` and `types` run as `check` spells them, and `build` is left to CI — as is the
#   consumer smoke test, which CI's `package` job runs on every pull request. This used to
#   run the whole `verify` here: ~60s and all 2,500 tests on every push, and two unrelated
#   load-sensitive tests failed pushes that had nothing to do with them (2026-09-23).
# ⚠️ "$@" CARRIES GIT'S REMOTE NAME, and stdin the pushed refs: the base comes from those.
# ⚠️ THE WORKSPACE PATH, for the reason in pre-commit.
bun packages/config/bin/hooks.ts pre-push "$@" || exit 1
